# Direct runtime dependencies of the backend; development/test ones are in requirements-dev.in.
# Edit the .in files, never a lock. All locks are hashed and compiled under Python 3.13.7
# (runtime.txt) with pip-tools 7.6.1 and the flags
#   --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --strip-extras --no-header
#
#   requirements.lock.txt              runtime; Render installs it through requirements.txt
#   requirements-dev.lock.txt          runtime + dev; CI (Linux)
#   requirements-dev.windows.lock.txt  the same versions plus Windows-only packages; local dev
#
# The Linux locks are compiled in python:3.13.7-slim from this directory:
#   pip-compile <flags> -o requirements.lock.txt requirements.in
#   pip-compile <flags> -o requirements-dev.lock.txt requirements-dev.in
# The Windows lock is compiled on Windows under 3.13.7, seeded from the Linux dev lock so the
# shared versions stay identical:
#   copy requirements-dev.lock.txt requirements-dev.windows.lock.txt
#   pip-compile <flags> -o requirements-dev.windows.lock.txt requirements-dev.in
# Install for local development:  pip install -r requirements-dev.windows.lock.txt
